# BUG-382: `n == "3"` with n an int passed -c and failed in Zig ("expected type 'str',
# found 'i64'"). Comparing a known string with a known number/bool is refused with a
# pointer to the conversion, the same narrowness as the concat check (BUG-218).
def main()
    var n = 3
    if n == "3"
        print("eq")
